      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the timing correlation is strange, the idea of commercial light bulbs actively eavesdropping and exfiltrating data via patterned light signals is a significant leap. Standard smart devices rely on IP communication, and while data leakage is a real concern, transmitting complex voice data through subtle, patterned light fluctuations is technically very difficult for consumer hardware. If you remain deeply concerned, you might consider temporarily relocating your communication devices away from the problematic bulbs or using a completely different, trusted lighting setup during sensitive conversations.",
